From 05c674c9132eb13e65e3fb6e9b4cf1cad1219fd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhao Zhili <zhilizhao@tencent.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:05:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/http: fix leak on failed proxy reconnect

After a 407 reply that asks for authentication, http_proxy_open()
closes the connection and reconnects. The reply headers parsed so far
may already have allocated state, for example the zlib stream set up
by Content-Encoding and new_location set by Location.

If the reconnect fails, returning directly skips http_proxy_close(),
and ffurl_closep() does not call url_close for a context that never
finished opening. Go through the fail label so that state is freed.

(cherry picked from commit 05c674c9132eb13e65e3fb6e9b4cf1cad1219fd5)
Upstream: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/05c674c9132eb13e65e3fb6e9b4cf1cad1219fd5
---
 libavformat/http.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/http.c b/libavformat/http.c
index d4dde2b..9325130 100644
--- a/libavformat/http.c
+++ b/libavformat/http.c
@@ -2490,7 +2490,7 @@ redo:
                                &h->interrupt_callback, NULL,
                                h->protocol_whitelist, h->protocol_blacklist, h);
     if (ret < 0)
-        return ret;
+        goto fail;
 
     authstr = ff_http_auth_create_response(&s->proxy_auth_state, auth,
                                            path, "CONNECT");
